{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-49,-34]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of the River Plate","date_start":"1939-12-13","date_end":"1939-12-17","date_label":"13-17 Dec 1939","theater":"South Atlantic","belligerents":"Royal Navy / Royal New Zealand Navy vs Kriegsmarine","outcome":"German pocket battleship scuttled off Montevideo","description":"British and New Zealand cruisers intercepted the German raider Admiral Graf Spee off the River Plate estuary; after taking refuge in Montevideo, her captain scuttled the ship rather than face the waiting Royal Navy force.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_River_Plate","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[17.56,68.42056]},"properties":{"name":"Battles of Narvik","date_start":"1940-04-10","date_end":"1940-04-13","date_label":"10 & 13 Apr 1940","theater":"Norwegian Sea (Ofotfjord)","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Kriegsmarine","outcome":"All ten German destroyers at Narvik destroyed","description":"Two Royal Navy destroyer actions in Ofotfjord, three days apart, destroyed the German destroyer force that had landed troops at Narvik during the Norwegian campaign.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battles_of_Narvik","coordinates_approximate":true}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-0.68889,35.71944]},"properties":{"name":"Attack on Mers-el-Kébir","date_start":"1940-07-03","date_end":"1940-07-03","date_label":"3 Jul 1940","theater":"Mediterranean Sea","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Vichy French Navy","outcome":"French squadron sunk or disabled at anchor","description":"To keep the Vichy French fleet from falling into German hands, a Royal Navy squadron attacked French warships at anchor near Oran, Algeria, killing over 1,200 French sailors.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attack_on_Mers-el-K%C3%A9bir","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[17.2075,40.45111]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Taranto","date_start":"1940-11-11","date_end":"1940-11-12","date_label":"11-12 Nov 1940","theater":"Mediterranean Sea","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Regia Marina","outcome":"Half the Italian battle fleet disabled in one night","description":"Fleet Air Arm biplane torpedo bombers launched from HMS Illustrious struck the Italian fleet at anchor in Taranto harbour, a raid later studied by Japan in planning Pearl Harbor.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Taranto","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[22,35.35]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Cape Matapan","date_start":"1941-03-27","date_end":"1941-03-29","date_label":"27-29 Mar 1941","theater":"Mediterranean Sea","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Regia Marina","outcome":"Decisive British victory; three Italian heavy cruisers sunk","description":"A British fleet under Andrew Cunningham, aided by codebreaking and radar, ambushed and destroyed a large Italian cruiser force off southern Greece.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Cape_Matapan","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-31.833,63.333]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of the Denmark Strait","date_start":"1941-05-24","date_end":"1941-05-24","date_label":"24 May 1941","theater":"Denmark Strait","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Kriegsmarine","outcome":"HMS Hood sunk; Bismarck damaged and forced toward France","description":"The German battleship Bismarck and cruiser Prinz Eugen engaged HMS Hood and HMS Prince of Wales; Hood exploded and sank within minutes, triggering the hunt for Bismarck.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Denmark_Strait","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-16.2,48.167]},"properties":{"name":"Sinking of the Bismarck","date_start":"1941-05-26","date_end":"1941-05-27","date_label":"26-27 May 1941","theater":"North Atlantic (Bay of Biscay)","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Kriegsmarine","outcome":"Bismarck crippled by aerial torpedo, then sunk by British battleships","description":"After a torpedo strike from a Fleet Air Arm Swordfish jammed her rudder, Bismarck was run down and sunk by British battleships and cruisers west of Brest, avenging the loss of HMS Hood three days earlier.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sinking_of_the_Bismarck","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[1.4,51.0]},"properties":{"name":"Channel Dash","date_start":"1942-02-11","date_end":"1942-02-13","date_label":"11-13 Feb 1942","theater":"English Channel","belligerents":"Kriegsmarine vs Royal Navy / RAF","outcome":"German squadron reached home ports despite British attacks","description":"The German battlecruisers Scharnhorst and Gneisenau, with the cruiser Prinz Eugen, ran the length of the English Channel from Brest to Germany in daylight, evading a scrambled British air and sea response.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Channel_Dash","coordinates_approximate":true}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[17.5,34.0]},"properties":{"name":"Second Battle of Sirte","date_start":"1942-03-22","date_end":"1942-03-22","date_label":"22 Mar 1942","theater":"Gulf of Sirte, Mediterranean Sea","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Regia Marina","outcome":"Outnumbered British escort fought off a stronger Italian force","description":"A heavily outgunned Royal Navy escort screened a Malta-bound convoy against an Italian battleship and cruiser force in a running battle in the Gulf of Sirte, using smoke and destroyer attacks to hold them off.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Battle_of_Sirte","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[111.0,-5.0]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of the Java Sea","date_start":"1942-02-27","date_end":"1942-02-27","date_label":"27 Feb 1942","theater":"Java Sea","belligerents":"ABDA Strike Force (US/UK/Netherlands/Australia) vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Decisive Japanese victory; most of the Allied squadron destroyed","description":"An Allied cruiser force attempting to stop a Japanese invasion convoy bound for Java was destroyed in a running battle, opening the way for the Japanese conquest of the Dutch East Indies.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Java_Sea","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-157.95,21.365]},"properties":{"name":"Attack on Pearl Harbor","date_start":"1941-12-07","date_end":"1941-12-07","date_label":"7 Dec 1941","theater":"Pacific Ocean (Oahu, Hawaii)","belligerents":"Imperial Japanese Navy vs United States","outcome":"US Pacific Fleet battleships crippled; US enters the war","description":"Carrier-launched Japanese aircraft attacked the US Pacific Fleet at anchor, sinking or damaging eight battleships and bringing the United States into the war.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attack_on_Pearl_Harbor","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[152.917,-10.483]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of the Coral Sea","date_start":"1942-05-04","date_end":"1942-05-08","date_label":"4-8 May 1942","theater":"Coral Sea","belligerents":"US Navy / RAN vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Tactical draw, strategic Allied victory; first carrier-vs-carrier battle","description":"The first naval battle fought entirely by carrier aircraft, with the opposing fleets never in sight of each other, halted the Japanese seaborne invasion of Port Moresby.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Coral_Sea","coordinates_approximate":true}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-178,30]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Midway","date_start":"1942-06-04","date_end":"1942-06-07","date_label":"4-7 Jun 1942","theater":"North Pacific Ocean, near Midway Atoll","belligerents":"US Navy vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Decisive US victory; four Japanese fleet carriers sunk","description":"US Navy carrier aircraft, aided by broken Japanese codes, sank four Japanese fleet carriers for the loss of one American carrier, a turning point of the Pacific War.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Midway","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[159.817,-9.133]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Savo Island","date_start":"1942-08-08","date_end":"1942-08-09","date_label":"8-9 Aug 1942","theater":"Solomon Islands (Guadalcanal)","belligerents":"US Navy / RAN vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Japanese night-fighting victory; four Allied cruisers sunk","description":"A Japanese cruiser force surprised the Allied screening force covering the Guadalcanal landings in a night action, sinking four cruisers without loss, one of the worst defeats in US Navy history.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Savo_Island","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[159.65,-9.1]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Cape Esperance","date_start":"1942-10-11","date_end":"1942-10-12","date_label":"11-12 Oct 1942","theater":"Solomon Islands (Guadalcanal)","belligerents":"US Navy vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"US victory","description":"US cruisers and destroyers ambushed a Japanese bombardment force off Guadalcanal at night, sinking a cruiser and a destroyer.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Cape_Esperance","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[159.895,-9.18611]},"properties":{"name":"Naval Battle of Guadalcanal","date_start":"1942-11-12","date_end":"1942-11-15","date_label":"12-15 Nov 1942","theater":"Solomon Islands (Guadalcanal)","belligerents":"US Navy vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"US victory; Japanese battleship bombardment mission defeated","description":"A series of fierce night surface actions off Guadalcanal, including a close-range melee that cost both sides admirals, turned back a Japanese attempt to bombard Henderson Field and reinforce the island.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naval_Battle_of_Guadalcanal","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[159.833,-9.2]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Tassafaronga","date_start":"1942-11-30","date_end":"1942-11-30","date_label":"30 Nov 1942","theater":"Solomon Islands (Guadalcanal)","belligerents":"US Navy vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Japanese tactical victory despite being outnumbered","description":"A small Japanese destroyer force running supplies to Guadalcanal inflicted heavy losses on a larger US cruiser squadron with a devastating torpedo attack.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Tassafaronga","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[29.0,73.25]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of the Barents Sea","date_start":"1942-12-31","date_end":"1942-12-31","date_label":"31 Dec 1942","theater":"Barents Sea","belligerents":"Kriegsmarine vs Royal Navy","outcome":"British escort drove off a superior German raiding force","description":"German heavy ships attempting to destroy convoy JW 51B were held off by its British destroyer escort until cruiser reinforcements arrived, embarrassing Hitler and hastening the German fleet's shift to submarine warfare.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Barents_Sea","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[22.25,75.817]},"properties":{"name":"Convoy PQ 17","date_start":"1942-06-27","date_end":"1942-07-10","date_label":"27 Jun - 10 Jul 1942","theater":"Arctic Ocean / Barents Sea","belligerents":"Allied Arctic convoy vs Kriegsmarine / Luftwaffe","outcome":"Convoy scattered on Admiralty order; two-thirds of its ships sunk","description":"Fearing an attack by the battleship Tirpitz, the Admiralty ordered convoy PQ 17 to scatter; U-boats and aircraft then picked off the unescorted merchant ships one by one in the worst Arctic convoy disaster of the war.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convoy_PQ_17","coordinates_approximate":true}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-42,55]},"properties":{"name":"Convoy ONS 5","date_start":"1943-04-29","date_end":"1943-05-06","date_label":"29 Apr - 6 May 1943","theater":"North Atlantic","belligerents":"Allied convoy escort vs Kriegsmarine U-boats","outcome":"Allied victory; a turning point in the Battle of the Atlantic","description":"A westbound convoy fought off sustained attacks by more than 30 U-boats in the mid-Atlantic air gap, sinking several submarines for the loss of a dozen merchantmen, a defeat that helped push German U-boats onto the defensive.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convoy_ONS_5","coordinates_approximate":true}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[28.25,72.517]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of North Cape","date_start":"1943-12-26","date_end":"1943-12-26","date_label":"26 Dec 1943","theater":"Barents Sea, off North Cape, Norway","belligerents":"Royal Navy vs Kriegsmarine","outcome":"British victory; Scharnhorst sunk","description":"The German battlecruiser Scharnhorst, sortieing against an Arctic convoy, was tracked by radar and sunk by a British battleship and cruiser force off North Cape, effectively ending German surface-fleet operations.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_North_Cape","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[130.0,20.0]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of the Philippine Sea","date_start":"1944-06-19","date_end":"1944-06-20","date_label":"19-20 Jun 1944","theater":"Philippine Sea","belligerents":"US Navy vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Decisive US victory; Japanese carrier air power destroyed","description":"US carrier aircraft and submarines destroyed the bulk of Japan's remaining carrier air groups in what American pilots nicknamed the 'Great Marianas Turkey Shoot.'","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Philippine_Sea","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-0.6,49.34]},"properties":{"name":"Normandy Landings (Operation Neptune)","date_start":"1944-06-06","date_end":"1944-06-06","date_label":"6 Jun 1944","theater":"English Channel, off Normandy","belligerents":"Allied naval forces vs Kriegsmarine / coastal defenses","outcome":"Allied landing fleet secured the beachhead","description":"The Allied invasion fleet of nearly 7,000 vessels bombarded German coastal defenses and landed troops across five Normandy beaches, opening the Western Front.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Normandy_landings","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[125.355,10.37]},"properties":{"name":"Battle of Leyte Gulf","date_start":"1944-10-23","date_end":"1944-10-26","date_label":"23-26 Oct 1944","theater":"Leyte Gulf, Philippines","belligerents":"US Navy / RAN vs Imperial Japanese Navy","outcome":"Decisive Allied victory; Japanese Navy loses its remaining offensive strength","description":"The largest naval battle of the war, fought in four separate actions across the Sibuyan Sea, Surigao Strait, off Cape Engano, and off Samar, shattered the Imperial Japanese Navy as an effective fighting force and saw the first organized kamikaze attacks.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Leyte_Gulf","coordinates_approximate":false}}
{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[128.067,30.367]},"properties":{"name":"Operation Ten-Go (Sinking of Yamato)","date_start":"1945-04-07","date_end":"1945-04-07","date_label":"7 Apr 1945","theater":"East China Sea","belligerents":"Imperial Japanese Navy vs US Navy","outcome":"Yamato sunk by US carrier aircraft before reaching Okinawa","description":"The battleship Yamato, the largest ever built, was sent on a one-way sortie to attack the Allied fleet off Okinawa and was sunk by waves of US carrier aircraft before reaching its target.","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Ten-Go","coordinates_approximate":false}}
